    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d665">

                <pb facs="0670" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/59.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Page to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 234]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the correspondence in regard
                    to the detention in Italy by the military authorities of the Reverend Dominick
                        Cassetta<anchor n="2" xml:id="d665-f1"/>
                    <pb facs="0671" n="555" xml:id="pg555"/> who, as already reported by the Consul
                    at Florence, left Italy early in December without awaiting official permission
                    to do so, I have the honor to enclose herewith a copy of a note received today
                    from the Royal Minister of Foreign Affairs upon the subject of his detention, as
                    well as upon the general question involved.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Nelson Page.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d665-a1.xml" xpointer="d665-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
